    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "The property is located in a private setting and has good views of the surrounding country side. \r\nThe property is steeped in family history, being held in the  family name for almost 300 years. \r\nA majestic two-storey farmhouse comprising of two bedrooms a functioning toilet and the surrounding land in a quant hidden site in beautiful West Wicklow. \r\n\r\nThe property is an absolute gem, it has Stunning Panoramic views of the Wicklow mountains located not far from Baltinglass town with the Irish army camp nearby. \r\nThe lands are laid out in 3 divisions of old pasture.\r\nThey extend to C. 2.19 acres with a partly renovated 2-storey farmhouse."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Kitchen/diner  3.54m x 3.13m\r\nLiving room 4.99m x 3.47m with solid fuel stove,  1 bedroom 3.4m x 3.2m,\r\nBathroom 2.39m x 1.95m, wash hand basin \r\nUpstairs:  1 bedroom 4.44m x 4.27m.\r\nThe house has been newly re-wired and partly refurbished.\r\nServices: Septic Tank."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: G"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "From Dublin take the N.81 road to Blessington, continue for approximately 19 km.\r\nTurn left for the Glen of Imaal continue to Knockanarrigan Cross roads, turn right for Michael Dwyer's Cottage.\r\nStay on that road until there is a sign for Ballinabarney Gap on the left, the property is on your left. Sign at Gate."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "VIEWING IS STRONGLY RECOMMENDED with the Sole Selling Agents: \r\nKinsella Auctioneers  Office 059 6481055 or mobile 0879781037\r\nEmail: office@kinsella.ie"
      }
    ],
